# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real .env.
APP_NAME=Urban Heat Intelligence API
ENVIRONMENT=development
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# --- Supabase + PostGIS ---
# From the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project URL + anon key: Dashboard → Project Settings → API
#   Database:               Dashboard → Project Settings → Database
#
# Connection notes (verified 2026-08):
#   * The direct host (db.<ref>.supabase.co) is IPv6-only — use the shared
#     pooler (IPv4) for local development and most deployments.
#   * NEW projects use the aws-1-* pooler hosts (aws-0-* hosts return
#     "tenant not found").
#   * User format on the pooler: postgres.<project-ref>
#   * Port 5432 = session mode (persistent backends, supports prepared
#     statements); port 6543 = transaction mode (serverless/edge only).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
